{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryafterflatmapping\/share()"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryAfterFlatMapping\/share()"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryAfterFlatMapping"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence that multicasts elements to multiple concurrent consumers."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"share"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncBroadcastSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that multicasts elements to multiple consumers concurrently."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This operator is an alias for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"broadcast()"},{"type":"text","text":", providing identical behavior."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It enables multicasting of values from the upstream sequence to multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"concurrent consumers without duplicating upstream work. A consumer receives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the elements the shared sequence reads from the upstream after the consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"creates its iterator; elements already read and handed out are not replayed."}]},{"text":"Example","type":"heading","anchor":"Example","level":2},{"code":["\/\/ Create an AsyncStream that emits 3 random values between 1 and 5","let upstream = AsyncStream<Int> { continuation in","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.finish()","}","","let sharedSequence = upstream.share()","","async let firstConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"First consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","async let secondConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"Second consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","\/\/ A consumer that subscribes after the shared sequence has handed out values misses them.","await firstConsumer.value","await secondConsumer.value"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/ShareSequence.swift#L113","fileName":"ShareSequence.swift"},"title":"share()","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"share"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","t